WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.770
One coin costs that much? I can't even afford a ticket in.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.419
That's the price of one whole coin. It's not what you have to pay each time.

00:00:13.419 --> 00:00:17.095
Bitcoin is a digital asset, and you can hold it in decimal amounts.

00:00:17.095 --> 00:00:18.960
You usually don't buy a whole one.

00:00:25.250 --> 00:00:30.717
One practice sum. Say one bitcoin is 50,000 USDT and you spend 100.

00:00:30.717 --> 00:00:36.510
Ignoring fees, that's 0. 002 bitcoin. This is not today's market price.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.700
And when the price moves?

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.145
The number of coins can stay the same, but their value goes up and down.

00:00:51.145 --> 00:00:54.600
Buying a little means risking less. It doesn't mean no risk.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.008
You can split it, but not every platform accepts any tiny order.

00:01:06.008 --> 00:01:10.353
Check the minimum amount and the fees. While you learn, use virtual funds.

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:11.410
No deposit needed.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.437
Do you have to buy a whole bitcoin? No.

00:01:17.437 --> 00:01:21.250
Remember: the price of one coin is not the price of getting started.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:31.960
Most trades are priced in USDT. But is USDT really a dollar? Next episode.

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:34.520
Understand first, then act.
